    {
      "sections": [
        {
          "kind": "intro",
          "paragraphs": [
            "Swiss main signals (system L) show a **Fahrbegriff**, a speed for the route: FB 1 = line speed, FB 2 = 40, FB 3 = 60, FB 5 = 90, FB 6 = 40 \"Kurze Fahrt\" (short distance to a Halt). **On the RhB** the same aspects mean FB 2 = 30, FB 3 = 45, FB 6 = 30, and there is no FB 5. Distant signals announce the next main signal; Luzern – Sursee also has **system N** signals with numbers. Speeds in km/h. Quadrant controls are from TheJAG's profiles: RhB Allegra (Berninalinie), RhB Ge 4/4 II (Arosalinie), SBB RABe 523 (Luzern – Sursee)."
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "systems",
          "title": "Safety systems",
          "cols": 4,
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "Integra-Signum",
              "full": "SBB intermittent train protection (TSW: ETCS STM level)",
              "summary": "A distant at Warnung (and a main signal at Kurze Fahrt) gives a buzzer and a yellow lamp: **acknowledge** at once (real: within 100 m or 5 s) or the train brakes. Passing a Halt brakes at once.",
              "where": "Luzern – Sursee (RABe 523)",
              "quadrant": "**Gear lever** = Signum reset"
            },
            {
              "name": "ETCS Level 1",
              "full": "TSW: Staff Responsible, then Full Supervision (the real line runs Limited Supervision)",
              "summary": "Select the level on the right display at a stand and confirm. Level 1 starts in SR (40 km/h to the first balise), then FS: speed monitoring and a braking curve with a warning tone. Level 0 only checks above 100 km/h.",
              "where": "Luzern – Sursee (RABe 523)",
              "quadrant": "**ENG 1** = confirm the level; left aux = ETCS on"
            },
            {
              "name": "ZSI-90 / ZS",
              "full": "RhB Zugsicherung (TSW); today ZSI 127",
              "summary": "Track magnets at a distant at Warnung and at Kurze Fahrt: two beeps and a flashing yellow lamp, press **ZS** or the emergency brake applies. Green lamp after a proceed aspect. Real RhB now runs balise-based ZSI 127.",
              "where": "Berninalinie, Arosalinie",
              "quadrant": "Allegra: **ENG 1** = ZS, left aux = ZSI on. Ge 4/4 II: **gear lever** = ZSI acknowledge (always on)"
            },
            {
              "name": "SiSte / deadman",
              "full": "Sicherheitssteuerung, Totmannpedal",
              "summary": "Allegra: SiSte, a timed vigilance like the SiFa: reset when the button lights. Ge 4/4 II: a deadman pedal, no timed alarm. RABe 523: none simulated.",
              "where": "Allegra, Ge 4/4 II",
              "quadrant": "Allegra: **gear lever** = SiSte reset, right aux = SiSte on. Ge 4/4 II: left aux = deadman cut-out (lit = cut out)"
            }
          ]
        },
